{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1050970337#2_1900123617","relevance":2,"reason":"This is another passage from the NPS Death Valley climate-change wildlife-study article. It gives supporting context about warming in other parks and Death Valley's vulnerability to climate change, but it does not directly quantify climate change at Zabriskie Point.","learned":"The NPS article repeatedly supports that Death Valley is relevant to climate-change impacts, but it is not a site-specific Zabriskie Point climate-change answer."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"death valley national park\" (+ \"climate trends\" \"climate change\" warming) (+ precipitation temperature))","reason":"Search for a more dedicated Death Valley National Park climate-trends document with temperature and precipitation evidence, which would be the strongest proxy for Zabriskie Point."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"death valley national park\" (+ \"climate trends\" \"climate change\" warming) (+ precipitation temperature))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1050970337#1_1900121535","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1572","rank":2,"snippet":"modern animal populations in Death Valley National Park, the project will be able to examine how rapid recent warming influences the geographic ranges of animal species, their diets, and their morphology. This is an unparalleled opportunity to learn how our changing climate has affected wildlife of Death Valley National Park. This information will also provide a new benchmark for comparison of future changes. UC Berkeley research completed similar research in Yosemite, Sequoia, Kings Canyon, and Lassen Volcanic National Parks. The re-survey of wildlife in these mountainous national parks revealed many changes in the distributions of mammals and birds after nearly 100 years. In Yosemite, where night-time <cover>temperature has increased by 5.4°F (3°C), half of the small mammal species showed significant changes in range, with an average upwards shift of approximately 1,640 feet (500 m) in elevation.\" , \"start_char\": 554.000000 , \"title\": \"Study to look at effects of climate change on wildlife - Death Valley National Park (</cover>U.S. National Park Service)\" , \"url\": \"https://www.nps.gov/deva/learn/news/grinell-wildlife-study.htm\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1050970337#2_1900123617","rank":1,"relevance":2}]}}
