{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"zabriskie point\" \"lake\" \"arid\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_508498143#9_900013587","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1583","rank":3,"snippet":"Death Valley in America’s Westward Expansion The Railroad and the Antelope Death Valley and Mojave Deserts’ Main Attractions Death Valley vs The Mojave Beauty of <cover>Zabriskie Point Prepare Your Car for a Desert Trip California Poppy Preserve Saddleback Butte Nearby Trips from the Death Valley and Mojave Deserts Solar Electrical Generation Calico Ghost Town More on Death Valley \" , \"segment\": \"The presence of tools in this arid area forcefully reminds a traveler of the changing weather patterns that affect plant, animal, and human habitation over long time spans. Tours of the site can be arranged through the Bureau of Land Management office in Barstow. Death Valley in America’s Westward Expansion During the westward expansion period in United States history, Death Valley was the scene of many heroic efforts, such as those of the Manly expedition. In 1849 William Manly was one of the first pioneers to succeed in traversing this unknown wilderness without dying of thirst. Stories of the Jayhawkers Trail from the Great Salt Lake </cover>in 1848 and the Darwin French Party Trail in 1860 are absorbing tales of human endurance in the midst of natural adversity. The interpretive center at Death ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_690527615#3_771752803","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_690527615#2_771751099","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
