{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1585"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_209635707#0_483604423","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1585","rank":3,"snippet":"at 1,530 feet, making it the highest point along the North Atlantic seaboard. Taking in a glowing sunrise from the mountaintops while overlooking the rocky coast of Maine is definitely worth waking up at the crack of dawn. Next Death Valley National Park, California © Vadim Startsev/Dreamstime.com Any desert region is made extra spectacular when the sun is near the horizon. And the different colors hitting the sand during sunrise at Death Valley National Park is a sight to see. The National Park Service suggests visitors see the sunrise from <cover>Zabriskie Point, which overlooks the golden-colored badlands of the Furnace Creek Formation. </cover>Other spots at Death Valley to watch the sun come up are Mesquite Flat Sand Dunes, Dantes View and Harmony Borax Works. Next Agra, India (Taj Mahal) © Anna Dudko/Dreamstime.com Sunrise is a spectacle at the Taj Mahal — the early morning light turns the magnificent site a soft, golden color.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Best sunrise spots around the world\" , \"url\": \"https://www.theactivetimes.com/travel/most-spectacular-places-view-sunrise-world\"","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_690527615#3_771752803","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
